 # Changelog
 
+## 0.1.6 (unreleased)
+
+Additive (rightkit#421). Already present from 0.1.5: `CallContextExt::peer_executable()` (rightkit#175) and `validate_args_strict` (rightkit#515).
+
+- `BoundedToolbox` (`bounded` module): `Toolbox` calls on worker threads with a time limit and an in-flight cap. `call` and `call_polled` (also ends on an external cancel signal) return a retryable `ERR_TIMEOUT` once the limit passes and cancel the call's `CancelToken`; a worker is counted in flight until its tool really returns, so a tool that ignores cancellation is visible through `stuck_workers()` and, at `max_in_flight` (default 4), new calls get a retryable `ERR_BUSY`. A panicking tool is `ERR_PANICKED` and frees its slot. A host that prefers to restart on a stuck tool checks `stuck_workers()`. New constants `ERR_TIMEOUT`, `ERR_BUSY`, `ERR_PANICKED`, `DEFAULT_MAX_IN_FLIGHT`.
+- Feature `mcp` (off by default; pulls `rightkit-mcp` 0.7): `ToolboxProvider::new(Arc<Toolbox>, Caller)` implements `rightkit_mcp::ToolProvider` for one caller. `tools/list` is `Toolbox::list_for`, `readOnlyHint` is true for `Effect::Observe`, and every `tools/call` passes the toolbox gate; unknown tool is `ToolNotFound`, any other `ToolError` is a tool-level failure carrying `{code, message, retryable}`, and a non-object result is wrapped as `{"result": ...}`. `.bounded(timeout, max_in_flight)` runs calls through `BoundedToolbox`, and a client's `notifications/cancelled` ends the wait (`call_with_handle`).
+- Resource declaration for the worker threads in `Cargo.toml` metadata.
+
 ## 0.1.5 (2026-10-17)
 
 - Added: `validate_args_strict(schema, args)`: `validate_args` plus unknown-argument rejection (a schema without `additionalProperties` is strict; `true` or a schema object opens it). `validate_args` is unchanged. Closes the Pulse `Args::parse` gap (rightkit#515).
