@@ -1,5 +1,18 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.2.1 (unreleased)
+
+Additive.
+
+### Added (rightkit#421, deadline stdin read)
+
+- `StdinDeadline { first_byte, quiet }` (default 2 s and 400 ms, Membrane's reader), `read_payload_deadline(reader, &StdinDeadline)`, `PayloadReadError`, `HookEvent::from_reader_deadline`, `run_with_deadline` and `run_deadline`. A host that opens a hook's stdin and never writes or closes it now yields the fallback reply and exit 0 instead of a hung hook; a payload ends at EOF or after the quiet window. The read runs on one helper thread that stays blocked if the reader never returns (the process exits next). `from_reader` and `run_with` are unchanged. The `rightkit-mcp` per-version batch policy and the `rightkit-agent-tools` parts of #421 are in their own crates.
+
+### Added (rightkit#551, host-side runner, feature `host`)
+
+- New cargo feature `host` (off by default; pulls `regex`) and module `host`: `HookSpec { command, matcher, timeout }` with a whole-name regex matcher, `parse_hook_specs_json(json, &EventKind)` (Claude Code settings shape), `parse_hook_output(stdout, stderr, exit_code, &EventKind) -> ParsedHook` (permission allow/ask/deny, `updatedInput`, `additionalContext`, `systemMessage`, `decision: block`, `continue: false`, exit code 2), `fails_closed(&EventKind)` (`PreToolUse`), `HookChain::run(&HookEvent, &[HookSpec], &dyn ProcessLaunch) -> ChainReport { verdict, updated_input, additional_context, system_message, stop, results }`, and the `ProcessLaunch` seam with `ShellLauncher` (`sh -c` / `cmd /C`, no console window, capped output, timeout kill). Chain rules: serial, deny-wins (deny, block, ask, allow, pass), stop after the first deny or block, `updatedInput` passed to the next hook, fail closed on pre-effect events and open elsewhere. Reuses `EventKind` and `HookEvent`. A destructive-command guard and the registry stay with the product.
+- #533 (notice-only `compose_reply`) and #543 (Membrane wire types) shipped in 0.2.0. #534: receipts stay in Pulse (ruling on the issue); `ReceiptStore::membrane` from 0.2.0 is the shared layout.
+
 ## 0.2.0 (2026-10-17)
 
 - `compose_reply` keeps a notice-only reply: a `systemMessage` with no decision and no context prints `{"systemMessage": ...}` instead of nothing.
