index 30aefc6..f7bf86a 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-send/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-send/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,14 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.2.1 (unreleased)
+
+Additive (rightkit#407; #537 `Entry::open_reader` already shipped in 0.2.0).
+
+- Transport abstraction on the send side: `send::Transport` (`peer_label`, `prepare_upload`, `upload`, `cancel`), `TransportReply { status, body }`, `TcpTransport` (the existing pinned-TLS carrier) and `send::deliver_with(&dyn Transport, ...)`, which holds the whole send policy (prepare-upload request, partial accept, per-file upload, progress, cancel, status-to-error mapping) with no TCP or TLS rule. `deliver` is unchanged in signature and behaviour; it checks HTTPS and the pin, then calls `deliver_with` over `TcpTransport`. A mesh host implements `Transport` and gets the same policy. Unit tests with a non-TCP mock carrier.
+- Generic trust subject: `TrustStore` is now public. Its key was always an opaque string of 1 to 128 characters compared lowercase, so a non-TLS device id works as a subject; the type docs say so, and a host without a `Service` can open the store directly.
+- `_pulse-send._tcp` is already the Bonjour service type (feature `bonjour`).
+- Not in this release: the receive side over a non-TCP carrier, the `@rightkit/send-ui` package and the Tauri command adapter (see the issue).
+
 ## 0.2.0 (2026-10-17)
 
 - Added: `Entry::open_reader() -> io::Result<Box<dyn Read + Send>>`, a public reader over a prepared entry (file or message text), for a host that streams entries over its own transport (rightkit#537). `Entry.source` stays private.
